  "paragraph_replacements": {
    "SWEEP_ABSTRACT": "The largest mixed dolphin return occurred at H=1T with 6 birds: 91\u2192113 captures against same-H controls (+24.2%); it exceeded the best-tested dolphin-only return of 91. These are discovery-bank outcomes, not a confirmed optimum.",
    "SWEEP_MAP_OVERVIEW": "All 60 declared executions, eight exact anchor replays and physical/raw-event audits passed. Across the nine mixed settings, mean same-H dolphin effects were positive in 7, zero in 0 and negative in 2. Mixed dolphin food ranged from 1.42 to 2.35 captures per dolphin over 36T. Figure 3 retains the entire map, not only its largest response.",
    "SWEEP_D_RESULTS": "The largest observed mixed dolphin return was at H=1T and 6 gannets, chosen by mixed mean food with fewer-bird and smaller-H tie rules. Across four schools, D-only and mixed totals were 91 and 113 (+24.2%); school differences were +4, +9, +4, +5 fish. The equal-school mean same-H change was +0.46 captures per dolphin per 36T, with pointwise 95% interval [+0.33, +0.65]. This in-sample selection is exploratory.",
    "SWEEP_G_RESULTS": "Mean count-matched per-bird effects were positive in 5 of nine settings, zero in 2 and negative in 2. At the selected dolphin-return setting, the mean gannet change was +0.54 captures per bird per 36T, interval [-0.38, +1.33]; raw gannet school differences were -5, +6, +2, +10. Both species gained in 3/4 schools there. At H=2T with 6 birds, dolphins changed 86\u2192103 and gannets 24\u219253, with both gaining in all four schools. Its dolphin interval against the stronger best-H benchmark crossed zero.",
    "SWEEP_BEST_RESULTS": "The highest across-school dolphin-only mean occurred at H=1T, with 91 captures across four schools. The selected mixed setting produced 113 (+24.2%), a mean change of +0.46 captures per dolphin per 36T against this stronger benchmark, interval [+0.33, +0.65]. The bootstrap reselects H within each school-vector draw. This is the best tested herding minimum for the retained rule, not an optimum across all dolphin behaviour.",
    "SWEEP_STATE_RESULTS": "Across all 12 dolphin-bearing settings, equal-school time-mean live-fish r90 ranged from 7.42 to 9.76 model units, while mean outward-moving fractions ranged from 0.104 to 0.366. Figure 4 shows every school and H, with no selected post-dive window. These state summaries are conditional on surviving fish and observed nonempty frames; they do not certify whole-school containment or isolate the effect of bird disturbance.",
    "SWEEP_CONTACT_RESULTS": "At H=1T and 6 birds, pooled dolphin eligible contacts changed from 130 to 156, launches from 251 to 267, and food from 91 to 113 across the same four schools. These descriptive changes occurred under the same conditional success rule.",
    "SWEEP_INTERPRETATION": "The map shows 7/9 positive mean same-H dolphin responses within four known schools. Its largest mixed return exceeded the best-tested D-only benchmark (113 versus 91 captures). That comparison includes selection and small-sample uncertainty; the full response map and school points are needed to assess it.",
    "SWEEP_CONCLUSION": "The original shared-rule pilots showed dolphin gains of 17.1% and 16.1%. The declared map now reports all nine mixed regimes and their controls: 7 have positive mean same-H dolphin effects, with the largest mixed return at H=1T and 6 birds (91\u2192113 against same-H D-only). These are conditional discovery-bank results; numerical sensitivity and held-out validation remain unresolved."
